                <pb facs="0129" n="41" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg41"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.5151/129: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morgan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-03-10T13:00:00-02:00">March 10, 1933—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 10—12:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>33. Department’s telegram No. 37, February 21, 5 p.m. Director of Exchange Bank
                    of Brazil,<anchor n="29" xml:id="d42-f1"/> who speaks for Minister of Finance,
                    tells me that pending the liquidation of the present Rothschild short-term loan
                    within the next 3 months he is negotiating with Stefani, Rothschild’s
                    representative here at present, for a long-term loan which will be applied to
                    alleviating accumulated commercial exchange. Bank is paying 20,000 pounds
                    (sterling) a day under the present short-term loan which will be reduced to
                    8,000 pounds (sterling) a day under the short [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >long?</hi>] term. This statement the exchange director has repeated to
                    reliable witnesses including Mallet-Prevost of New York City with whom he had an
                    interview last week.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morgan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d42-f1" n="29" xml:id="d42-f1-content">
